items/lem-the-order-topology-on-an-ordinal.md:66:[L1] $\gamma$ is the set of the ordinals below it; membership is a strict linear order on it, $\alpha \le \beta$ abbreviates "$\alpha \in \beta$ or $\alpha = \beta$", and $\alpha \subseteq \beta$ holds exactly when $\alpha \le \beta$ ([[def-ordinal]], [[lem-ordinal-basics]], [[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]], [[def-partial-order]]).
