items/ex-the-rationals-are-totally-disconnected-and-not-discrete.md:103:- **Local connectedness fails for a structural reason, not a delicate one.** In any totally disconnected space the only candidates for a connected neighbourhood are singletons, so local connectedness at $x$ is equivalent to $\{x\}$ being open. Hence a totally disconnected space is locally connected exactly when it is discrete, and step 3.1 is that observation applied to $\mathbb{Q}$.
